The upgrade to yoagent 0.25.5 is committed as b58e4329, and Cargo.lock now pins 0.25.5. The one integration test that was making every session throw away the dependency update, doc_version_claims, now passes. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test run are clean: 6599 passed, 0 failed.

What changed upstream, compared file by file: I diffed the 0.25.2 and 0.25.5 crate sources. Only four source files changed: three in decision/ (the ToolGate code) and tools/search.rs.
• ToolGate (0.25.4): yoyo doesn't use it. Nothing in src/ mentions ToolGate or decision::.
• `search` (0.25.5): it now passes --no-config to rg and clears RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH and GREP_OPTIONS for the child. It also finds rg without which, and a search that ends abnormally is now an error instead of "No matches".
• 0.25.3: docs only. It's the release that ships the yoagent skill inside the crate.

Every file the 15 markers cite (sub_agent.rs, agent_loop.rs, extension.rs, provider/traits.rs, the Usage and gasp code) is byte-identical, so all the quoted line numbers still hold.

The 15 markers: I re-read each paragraph against 0.25.5. None of them makes a claim about search, ripgrep config, ToolGate or "No matches", so none needed rewriting and all 15 are just bumped to 0.25.5. The commit body lists each one with "unchanged by 0.25.3–0.25.5".

Also in the lock: cargo moved a few Windows-only crates from windows-sys 0.61.2 back to 0.59.0. It doesn't affect Linux builds. I didn't take the other optional dependency bumps.

